Package: god
Title: A Grammar of Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("psychometrician", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "psychometrician@gmail.com")
Description: One small vocabulary for manipulating tables, spelled the same way
    in R, in Python, and on a cluster. A pipeline is checked before any of it
    runs, so a bad column is reported at the step that names it rather than
    failing partway through. The grammar owns the words, the checking and the
    messages; an engine underneath does the work.
License: Apache License (== 2.0)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.0)
Imports:
    DBI,
    duckdb
Suggests:
    knitr,
    pkgload
